      "message": "[warning] Line 80: 🟡 `ContextMenu.menu: null` disables Qt’s built-in context-menu entry points (including keyboard-triggered context menu via Menu key / Shift+F10), while the custom menu is only opened from `onReleased` right-click. This introduces an accessibility regression for keyboard users. Add an explicit keyboard path (for example, handling `Keys.onMenuPressed` or a `Shortcut` for `StandardKey.ContextMenu`) that opens the same Jami menu at the caret/selection location, and mirror that behavior in the other text components changed in this patch.",
